---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — HealthyBMICheck.com"
  description="Privacy policy for HealthyBMICheck.com. Calculators run locally in your browser by default; an optional Save & Track account feature is available for users who want to track their history."
  canonical="https://healthybmicheck.com/privacy"
>
<div class="content">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="date">Last updated: July 2026</p>

  <p>HealthyBMICheck.com ("we", "our", or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard information when you visit our website.</p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>By default, HealthyBMICheck.com does not collect or store any personal health data you enter into our calculators. All calculations are performed locally in your browser, and your height, weight, and results are never transmitted to or stored by us — unless you choose to use the optional "Save & Track" feature described below.</p>

  <h2>Optional Account Feature: Save &amp; Track</h2>
  <p>Some calculators (currently the BMI Calculator and Asian BMI Calculator) offer an optional "Save this result &amp; track my progress" feature. This is entirely opt-in — if you don't use it, no account is created and no health data ever leaves your browser.</p>
  <p>If you choose to use this feature, here is exactly what happens:</p>
  <ul style="color:var(--ink2);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin:8px 0 14px 20px;">
    <li><strong>No passwords.</strong> You sign in with a one-time "magic link" sent to your email. We never ask for or store a password.</li>
    <li><strong>What we store:</strong> your email address, and — only if you tick the box to save your history — the weight, height, BMI, and category from the result you chose to save, along with the date it was recorded.</li>
    <li><strong>Two separate consent choices:</strong> saving your history is required to use this feature; receiving occasional email reminders/tips is a completely separate, optional choice. Ticking one does not tick the other.</li>
    <li><strong>Where it's stored:</strong> in a Cloudflare D1 database associated with this website. Login links are single-use and expire after 15 minutes.</li>
    <li><strong>Session cookie:</strong> once you sign in, we set a strictly-necessary cookie (<code>session</code>) to keep you signed in for up to 30 days. This cookie is only used for authentication — not for advertising or tracking.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Deleting your data:</strong> you can request deletion of your account and all saved health records at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@healthybmicheck.com">hello@healthybmicheck.com</a> from the email address associated with your account. We will delete your data within a reasonable timeframe and confirm once done.</p>
  <p>This feature is intended for adult users tracking their own health data. Our Child BMI Calculator offers a separate, parent-consent version of this feature — see below.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and Analytics</h2>
  <p>We may use cookies and similar tracking technologies to analyse website traffic and improve your experience. This may include Google Analytics, which collects anonymised usage data such as pages visited and time on site.</p>

  <h2>Google AdSense &amp; Advertising</h2>
  <p>This website uses Google AdSense to display advertisements. Google AdSense uses cookies and similar tracking technologies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites on the internet.</p>
  <p>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to this site. You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>.</p>

  <h2>Your Cookie Choices</h2>
  <p>Most web browsers allow you to control cookies through their settings. You can choose to block or delete cookies, though doing so may affect your experience on this and other websites. For more information, visit <a href="https://www.allaboutcookies.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">allaboutcookies.org</a>.</p>

  <h2>Data Retention</h2>
  <p>For visitors who do not use the optional Save &amp; Track feature: calculator inputs (height, weight, age) are processed entirely in your browser and are never transmitted to or stored by us.</p>
  <p>For users who opt into Save &amp; Track: your email address and saved health records are retained until you request deletion (see above), or until your account has been inactive for an extended period, at which point we may delete it as part of routine data minimisation. Analytics data collected by Google Analytics is retained according to Google's own data retention policies.</p>

  <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
  <p>Our website may contain links to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites and encourage you to review their privacy policies.</p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>Our website is not directed at children under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children.</p>
  <p>Our Child BMI Calculator offers an optional feature for a <strong>parent or legal guardian</strong> to save their child's BMI-for-age percentile result and track it over time. This is explicitly consented to by the adult, not the child:</p>
  <ul style="color:var(--ink2);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin:8px 0 14px 20px;">
    <li>The account is created with the <strong>parent's</strong> email address — the child never provides their own contact information or creates an account.</li>
    <li>The consent checkbox explicitly states "I am the parent or legal guardian of this child."</li>
    <li>We do not require or ask for the child's full name. Parents may optionally enter a short nickname purely to tell multiple children apart in their own account — this is optional and never required.</li>
    <li>Data saved is limited to what's needed for the growth calculation: BMI, percentile, age, and sex. No other information about the child is collected.</li>
    <li>The same deletion rights described above apply — a parent can delete this data at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies We Use</h2>
  <p>This website uses the following types of cookies:</p>
  <ul style="color:var(--ink2);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin:8px 0 14px 20px;">
    <li><strong>Google Analytics cookies</strong> — Used to analyse how visitors use our site. Data is anonymised and aggregated. Opt out via <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Opt-out</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Google AdSense cookies</strong> — Used to serve relevant advertisements. Manage ad personalisation at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Functional cookies</strong> — Session cookies that remember your unit preferences (metric/imperial). These expire when you close your browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Authentication cookie</strong> — If you use the optional Save &amp; Track feature, a strictly-necessary <code>session</code> cookie keeps you signed in for up to 30 days. Not used for advertising.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your Rights (GDPR &amp; CCPA)</h2>
  <p><strong>EU / EEA users (GDPR):</strong> You have the right to access, correct, or request deletion of any personal data we hold. As we do not collect or store personal health data, this primarily applies to contact information you voluntarily provide. Contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@healthybmicheck.com">hello@healthybmicheck.com</a> to exercise these rights.</p>
  <p><strong>California users (CCPA):</strong> We do not sell personal information. California residents have the right to know what personal information is collected, request deletion, and opt out of sale. Contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@healthybmicheck.com">hello@healthybmicheck.com</a> for any privacy requests.</p>

  <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>This website uses the following third-party services, each governed by their own privacy policies:</p>
  <ul style="color:var(--ink2);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin:8px 0 14px 20px;">
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google AdSense Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Web3Forms Privacy Policy</a> (contact form processing)</li>
    <li><a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resend Privacy Policy</a> (sends the login-link emails for users who opt into Save &amp; Track)</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a> (website hosting, and database storage for users who opt into Save &amp; Track)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. When we do, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of the website after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@healthybmicheck.com">hello@healthybmicheck.com</a> or via our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
</div>
<div style="padding-bottom: 20px;"></div>
</Base>
